' Agent-driven ArchiMate rendering pipeline (the post's core claim)
@startuml
top to bottom direction
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 8
sprite $app jar:archimate/application-component
sprite $svc jar:archimate/application-service
sprite $sys jar:archimate/technology-system-software
sprite $gap jar:archimate/gap-filled

title "Agent-driven diagram pipeline: text-in, standards-compliant diagram-out"

rectangle "EA agent\n(TOGAF ADM / OAA phase)" as agent <<$app>> #Application
rectangle "Emit .puml\nArchiMate stereotypes\n+ relationship macros" as emit <<$svc>> #Application
rectangle "java -jar plantuml.jar\nheadless, no display, no GUI" as jar <<$sys>> #Technology
rectangle ".puml source\n(diff-able, versioned,\nagent-parseable)" as src <<$svc>> #Technology
rectangle "SVG / PNG\ncommitted to diagrams/" as out <<$svc>> #Technology

agent --> emit : structured model
emit --> jar : text
jar --> out : renders

note bottom of src
  Two audiences, one artifact:
  agents read the .puml,
  architects review the PNG.
  Neither is an afterthought.
end note

rectangle "Fails this pipeline:\nMermaid (no ArchiMate shapes)\nD2 (generic layout only)\nArchi (needs display + GUI)" as fail <<$gap>> #Application

src .. fail : wrong tool
@enduml
